    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ab0bbbb5641a75e0bf2b140fa50b9926",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1849,
    "chunk_text": "He raised serious suspicions about former President Maithripala Sirisena, who was also serving as Defence Minister during the attacks.\n\nHe also questioned the timing of Sirisena\u2019s sudden departure to Singapore prior to the attacks, without naming an Acting Minister, despite the existence of advance intelligence warnings.\n\nHe went on to accuse three former Presidents\u2014Maithripala Sirisena, Gotabaya Rajapaksa, and Ranil Wickremesinghe of protecting Jayawardena despite widespread allegations and public outrage during the past six years. \u201cThere is a strong feeling that these three leaders had something to hide and they used Jayawardena\u2019s continued presence in the Police to do just that,\u201d he alleged.\n\nRev. Fr. Krishantha called on the Government to take bold steps in exposing the full truth. \u201cThe new Government has a duty to uncover what those in power tried to hide. The people deserve to know the truth. The victims deserve justice,\u201d he asserted.\n\nHe insisted that justice must be served irrespective of rank or political status. \u201cWhether it is a former President or a senior officer, anyone responsible must be held accountable in a Court of law. No one is above justice,\u201d he added.\n\nRev. Fr. Krishantha called for the harshest possible punishment for those convicted of direct or indirect involvement in the Easter Sunday bombings on 21 April 2019 which targeted churches and hotels across Sri Lanka, killing over 260 people and injuring hundreds more.\n\n\u201cIn my opinion, even a life sentence is not enough. For a crime of this magnitude, the death penalty is what justice demands,\u201d he said, expressing the depth of the Catholic Church\u2019s continued grief and demand for accountability.\n\nThe coordinated Easter Sunday suicide bombings remain one of the deadliest terrorist incidents in the country\u2019s post-war history."
  },
