    "chunk_size_bytes": 625,
    "chunk_text": "US experts through the Economic Co-operation Administration (ECA), however, had spread instability by advising Keynesian remedies and central bank credit funded development banks including to Japan which was hit by triple digit inflation, until Dodge came.\n\nAs inflation returned this  to Japan, as desired by macro-economists for many years the Liberal Democrats lost their parliamentary majority and a new nationalist party made inroads.\n\nTaiwan\u2019s exchange rate was stabilized by a student of Hayek at the London School of Economics. Singapore was also fixed by Goh Keng Swee who had studied at LSE. (Colombo/July21/2025)"
