    "md5": "5bff70416f62500f41f31fdddf837b93",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1318,
    "chunk_text": "A probe eclipsed by sideshows\n\nThere seems to be no end in sight to the ongoing probe into the 2019 Easter Sunday terror attacks. President Anura Kumara Dissanayake pledged to make a revelation about the carnage before its sixth anniversary, which fell last April, but that promise went unfulfilled. Subsequently, Public Security Minister Ananda Wijepala made a statement in Parliament and that left the public none the wiser. It was a classic case of the proverbial mountains in labour delivering a mouse. He claimed that TMVP\u2008leader and former State Minister Sivanesathurai Chandrakanthan alias Pilleyan had prior knowledge of the terror attacks while in prison. Why has he been singled out? In the aftermath of the terrorist attacks in 2019, the then Minister Harin Fernando said his father, an ordinary citizen, had received information about the impending terror strikes. Many police and intelligence officers were also privy to a warning about the attacks.\n\nSadly, one can argue\u2014with due respect to the victims and the campaigners for justice\u2014that the ongoing probe into the Easter Sunday tragedy has come to resemble a \u2018mega teledrama\u2019 with new episodes added to it endlessly. The Channel 04 programme on the Easter Sunday attacks is a case in point; it is full of sensational, unsubstantiated claims."
  },
