    "chunk_text": "On Wednesday (23) Minister of Public Security Ananda Wijepala told Parliament, in answer to a question raised by SJB MP Rohini Kaviratne, that no records were available about the 1989 attack on the Dalada Maligawa during the JVP\u2019s reign of terror, except the arrest of six female suspects. On several occasions, the JVP has denied any involvement in the terror attack on the Dalada Maligawa. But Neranjan Wijeratne, who was the Diyawadena Nilame at the time of the attack, has vehemently rejected the JVP\u2019s denials. When the issue resurfaced in the run-up to the 2001 general election, Wijeratne was quoted by The Island (on 25 November 2001) as saying that the JVP was responsible for that terror strike which claimed five lives.\n\nIt is public knowledge that some UNP politicians ran dungeons where suspected JVP activists were tortured and murdered. Some of them and their family members are still in politics. Curiously, the JVP MPs who remember the UNP\u2019s crimes such as torture and extrajudicial killings suffer memory losses when questions are raised about their party\u2019s savage terror campaign in the past. They have also forgotten their leader, Rohana Wijeweera, who was arrested, tortured, shot and cremated alive, according to some eyewitnesses. The JVP-led NPP government has ordered a CID probe into the disappearance of Lalith and Kugan but ignored calls for an investigation into the extrajudicial execution of its founding leader!"
