    "chunk_text": "It is public knowledge that some UNP politicians ran dungeons where suspected JVP activists were tortured and murdered. Some of them and their family members are still in politics. Curiously, the JVP MPs who remember the UNP\u2019s crimes such as torture and extrajudicial killings suffer memory losses when questions are raised about their party\u2019s savage terror campaign in the past. They have also forgotten their leader, Rohana Wijeweera, who was arrested, tortured, shot and cremated alive, according to some eyewitnesses. The JVP-led NPP government has ordered a CID probe into the disappearance of Lalith and Kugan but ignored calls for an investigation into the extrajudicial execution of its founding leader!\n\nThe police, who go out of their way, after every regime change, to reopen probes into the crimes committed by the previous governments, have also suffered a memory loss. They have not investigated the massacre of their own men, reportedly numbering 600, who surrendered to the LTTE in 1990, in the Eastern Province; they were led into the jaws of death by the then UNP government in the name of \u2018peace\u2019.\n\nSri Lankan voters also have a history of selective memory lapses, which have stood violent, corrupt politicians in good stead. They forget politicians\u2019 crimes, past and present, when they vote in elections. They are gluttons for punishment. It is said that a nation gets the government it deserves.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
  },
