    "md5": "f655a040e2c6ace09f8f92d0ed4a550c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1924,
    "chunk_text": "Uber rolls into Jaffna \u2013 rides and eats now available in Northern Province\n\nUber, Sri Lanka\u2019s ride-hailing and delivery platform, today announced the launch of its services in Jaffna, marking a significant milestone in its nationwide expansion. With this launch in the Northern province, the residents as well as visitors will now have access to safer, affordable rides and on-demand food and grocery delivery, all at the tap of a button. It will also contribute to the local economy by creating new earning opportunities for local drivers, delivery partners, and merchants.\n\nAs part of this expansion, Tamil language support has been rolled out across the country, making the app experience even more accessible to millions of Tamil-speaking Sri Lankans.\n\nWhether it\u2019s a ride to Jaffna University, a weekend visit to Nallur Kandaswamy Temple, or a trip to the city\u2019s beloved library, Uber Rides will make it easier to move around Jaffna quickly and affordably. And with Uber Eats now live in the city, locals and visitors can enjoy Jaffna\u2019s most loved dishes like crab curry, kool, and dosai, from neighbourhood favourites such as Lavin\u2019s Vegetarian Family Restaurant, Selam RR Biriyani, Akshathai Restaurant, and Mangos Indian Veg, all delivered to their doorstep with just a few taps.\n\nUber Eats launches with the widest-ever restaurant and grocery selection Jaffna has seen across any delivery platform. With popular local eateries and trusted grocery partners on the app, and a strong network of delivery partners across the city, Uber Eats will offer a faster and more reliable delivery experience than what customers have been used to.\n\nVision Care Hearing Solutions launches dedicated audiology unit in Panadura\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
