    "description": "Sri Lanka\u2019s JKCG says in discussions with authorities over detained Chinese BYDs",
    "url_metadata": "https://economynext.com/sri-lankas-jkcg-says-in-discussions-with-authorities-over-detained-chinese-byds-233474/",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "economynextcom",
    "time_ut": 1753803660.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-07-29-economynextcom-42c81018-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "71b856252d6bc62746140251242f0e1e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2029,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s JKCG says in discussions with authorities over detained Chinese BYDs\n\nECONOMYNEXT \u2013 Sri Lanka\u2019s authorized distributor of BYD vehicles John Keells CG Auto (Pvt) Ltd (JKCG) is \u201cactively engaged\u201d in discussions with the relevant government authorities to clarify an issue with regard motor power, the company said.\n\nSri Lanka Customs has detained around 1,000 Chinese-made BYD electric vehicles that arrived in the island this month over a motor capacity issue which is used to calculate taxes, official sources have said.\n\nCustoms have been declared a motor output of 100 kiloWatts, based on the manufacturers rating where output is limited to 100kW with a reduction is performance.\n\n\u201cWe would like to reassure our key stakeholders and the public that\u2026 the vehicles in question imported directly from the manufacturer, BYD in China, are 100 kW models,\u201d the JKCG said in a statement.\n\n\u201cThese are identical to the models offered for sale in some other international markets such as Singapore,\u201d it said.\n\n\u201cThe motor power of these vehicles has been verified through test reports issued by BYD in China and further certified by an independent testing body. As a responsible corporate, JKCG also confirms that all vehicle imports have been conducted in full compliance and applicable local regulations.\u201d\n\n\u201cWe remain committed to transparency and are cooperating fully with the authorities to provide all clarifications regarding this matter. JKCG will continue to keep its customers and the other stakeholders informed as the matter progresses.\u201d\n\nBYD sells 100kW models of its Atto 3 model in some markets, where the authorities have allowed the technology.\n\nBYD in Singapore sells an Atto 3 model with a 100kW rated motor to conform to what is called a Category A certificate of entitlement in Singapore, according to the company website.\n\nA lower rated motor means its performance will be lower, and for example may not be able to accelerate as quickly as the one with the higher output motor."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-07-29-economynextcom-42c81018",
    "num": "economynextcom-42c81018",
    "date_str": "2025-07-29",
    "description": "Sri Lanka\u2019s JKCG says in discussions with authorities over detained Chinese BYDs",
    "url_metadata": "https://economynext.com/sri-lankas-jkcg-says-in-discussions-with-authorities-over-detained-chinese-byds-233474/",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "economynextcom",
