    "chunk_size_bytes": 1859,
    "chunk_text": "38th Annual Conference of the Organisation of Professional Associations of Sri Lanka\n\nThe Organisation of Professional Associations of Sri Lanka (OPA), established in 1975, serves as the apex body representing Sri Lanka\u2019s professional community. With 52 member associations spanning 34 disciplines, including Law, Medicine, Engineering, Accountancy, Supply Chain Management, Architecture, and Banking ,the OPA is a unifying platform for over 60,000 professionals.\n\nThe OPA\u2019s core mission is to leverage the collective expertise of Sri Lanka\u2019s professionals to contribute to national development, foster professional excellence, and promote ethical leadership across sectors.\n\nWe are pleased to announce the 38th Annual Conference of the OPA, the signature event of our calendar, scheduled for the 19th and 20th of August 2025 at Cinnamon Life, Colombo.\n\nThis year\u2019s conference is of special significance as it will also feature the 4th National Apex Awards, honouring Sri Lanka\u2019s most exemplary professionals for their lifetime achievements and outstanding contributions to their respective fields and to the nation.\n\nThrough this media briefing, we aim to convey the theme, objectives, and national relevance of the conference while inviting widespread participation and collaboration from Sri Lanka\u2019s professional and business communities.\n\nIn the context of an evolving global landscape, this theme emphasizes the critical need for Sri Lanka\u2019s professionals and institutions to strengthen resilience, adapt dynamically, and lead transformation.\n\nThe conference will commence with an inaugural ceremony attended by over 300 distinguished professionals, representing member associations, academia, and industry.\n\nThe Guest of Honour will be Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma, Secretary to the Ministry of Finance, who will deliver the Keynote Address."
