    "md5": "769849a835731af8d347b43b7d3d52f1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1951,
    "chunk_text": "HNB General Insurance \u2018Celebrating Excellence 2025\u2019 honours exceptional staff and top-tier sales achievers\n\nHNB General Insurance (HNBGI), a leading player in Sri Lanka\u2019s general insurance sector, recently hosted its annual flagship event, \u2018Celebrating Excellence 2025\u2019, at Waters Edge, Battaramulla. The evening brought together staff and sales professionals from across the country in a unified celebration of dedication and achievement. HNBA and HNBGI Chairman Stuart Chapman graced the event as Chief Guest, joined by members of the Board of Directors \u2013 reinforcing the company\u2019s belief that people are the true engine behind its continued growth.\n\nThis year\u2019s gathering marked a meaningful chapter in HNB General Insurance\u2019s journey, recognizing not just business performance, but also the shared values, resilience, and commitment that drive the organization forward. The event celebrated team spirit across every level \u2013 from front-line sales to back-office support \u2013 highlighting the unity that powers HNBGI.\n\nAlongside the Platinum Club Sales Awards, which recognized 24 top achievers across national, zonal, cluster, and branch levels, the company also presented Long Service Awards to employees who have demonstrated years of loyalty and dedication. Chairman\u2019s Awards were conferred on individuals who showcased exceptional leadership, innovation, or impact \u2013 further underscoring HNB General Insurance\u2019s culture of appreciation.\n\nAdding to the celebrations, four Special Awards recognized outstanding accomplishments beyond traditional metrics. These included the HNBGI Cricket Team, champions of the MCA Division \u2018G\u2019 Tournament; Vimukthi Gamage, for representing Sri Lanka in the Rugby World Cup Asia Qualifiers; the HNBGI Quiz Team, winners of the Inter-Insurance/Broker Company Quiz Competition; and the In.She Woman Icon Award, presented under the company\u2019s `In.She` initiative for female empowerment."
