    "md5": "478bad635730ccc99ca2f572131cefb2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 680,
    "chunk_text": "And more than a dozen countries have tariff rates that are higher than 15%, either because they agreed to a trade framework with the United States or because Trump sent their leaders a letter dictating a higher tariff. The senior administration official said those countries have among the highest trade deficits with the United States.\n\nThe new tariff regime will not go into effect Friday, as expected. Instead, the tariffs will be implemented on August 7 to give Customs and Border Protection sufficient time to make the necessary changes to collect the new duties.\n\nAccordingly, the US president announced adjustments to some of those reciprocal tariffs ahead of its deadline."
