    "chunk_text": "CEAT Kelani recognised once again at National Business Excellence Awards 2025\n\nCEAT Kelani Holdings, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading manufacturer of pneumatic tyres and the company behind the country\u2019s highest-selling tyre brand CEAT, has once again been recognised for business excellence, emerging as Joint Runner-Up in the \u2018Manufacturing \u2013 Other Sector\u2019 category at the National Business Excellence Awards (NBEA) 2025.\n\nCompeting in the Extra-Large category for enterprises with annual revenue exceeding Rs 10 billion, CEAT Kelani\u2019s performance at this year\u2019s competition reaffirms its standing as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most professionally and efficiently managed businesses.\n\nNow in its 20th year, the NBEA is the flagship awards programme of the National Chamber of Commerce of Sri Lanka, which celebrates outstanding business achievements and promotes global standards of excellence across the country\u2019s corporate landscape. CEAT\u2019s continued success at this prestigious competition underscores the company\u2019s commitment to organisational excellence and its contribution to the national economy.\n\nThe evaluation criteria for the awards covered seven pillars of excellence: Strategy & Leadership, Corporate Governance, Capacity Building, Performance Management, Local and Global Market Reach, CSR and Environmental Sustainability, and Business & Financial Results.\n\nCEAT\u2019s submission highlighted its integrated Quality-Based Management (QBM) system, a proprietary Total Quality Management (TQM) framework which instils a culture of continuous improvement. The company\u2019s QBM philosophy is built around Customer Focus, People Focus, and Process Focus, ensuring that every employee contributes towards the achievement of business goals and delivery of superior value.\n\nPan Asia Bank posts strong performance with PAT of over Rs. 2.1 billion for 1H2025; increase of 110%\n\nUptick in stock market\u2019s fortunes following US import tariff reduction"
