    "chunk_text": "President Barack Obama was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize in 2009, but the US, under his watch, backed the invasion of Libya, making that country descend into a failed state, fractured by rival militias, extremist groups, arms traffickers, human smugglers and various other criminal gangs.\n\nIt may not be fair to deny Trump the credit for having stopped several conflicts that may otherwise have developed into full-blown wars, but shouldn\u2019t he intervene to stop the destruction of lives in Gaza before seeking the Nobel Peace Prize? As an ardent supporter of Israel, he is duty-bound to do everything in his power to save Palestinians\u2019 lives in Gaza. If he brings adequate pressure to bear on Israel, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu will have to stop his military campaign that harms civilians and allow aid to be distributed properly.\n\nEven the traditional US allies have found it difficult to ignore the situation in Gaza any longer. The UK has warned that it will formally recognise the state of Palestine in September due to the \u201cincreasingly intolerable\u201d situation in Gaza, unless Israel abides by a ceasefire and commits to a two-state solution in the Middle East. Canada and France have said they will do likewise. Some more western nations are expected to follow suit. This is a situation the US and Israel did not bargain for. President Trump has rebuked UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer for the UK plan to recognise Palestine, and reiterated his wholehearted support for Israel despite the ongoing atrocities against civilians in Gaza. And, the White House wants him awarded the Nobel Peace Prize!\n\nMeanwhile, one can argue that the Nobel Peace Prize lost its meaning when it was denied to Mahatma Gandhi five times. The Nobel Committee cited various reasons for its decision in question, but its subsequent reflections revealed regret. It was the greatest omission in the history of the prize, one of the committee Secretaries said in 2006."
